11. Using Caching for Faster Builds

Installing dependencies repeatedly wastes time.

Caching stores dependencies.

Example:

- uses: actions/cache@v4

For Node.js:

- uses: actions/cache@v4
  with:
    path: ~/.npm

Benefits:

Faster builds
Lower execution time
Reduced resource usage
12. Multi-Job Workflows

Multiple jobs can work together.

Example:

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

  test:
    needs: build
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

Flow:

Build
   ↓
Test
   ↓
Deploy

The test job starts only after build completes.

